      "writtenOn": "2021-09-22T16:33:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of switching on/off on each transaction, we can call i2c_raw_mode(1) for all ports in i2c_init and call i2c_raw_mode(0) before leaving the main(). It will not only remove the switching overhead but also allow us to handle errors from i2c_raw_mode properly (i.e. try again, print error, or assert).\n\nWe can add something like i2c_prepare_task_mode to i2c_controller.c. What do you think?",
